et via OpenRouter for improved performance, new /report command for session summaries, and --chat-language switch for multi-language support.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Release</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-05</span></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"product-name\">Continue</span> — Version 1.3.38-vscode\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Config.yaml fixes, workspace directory filtering capabilities, and support for .continue/configs directory structure.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Release</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-04</span></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"product-name\">GitHub Copilot</span> — Copilot SDK Public Preview\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        GitHub Copilot SDK entered public preview, allowing developers to build custom integrations and extend Copilot capabilities.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Announcement</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-02</span></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"product-name\">Windsurf</span> — Version 1.9600.41: Adaptive Model Router\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Adaptive model router for intelligent task routing to optimal models, plus GPT-5.4 mini integration and various model updates.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Release</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-07</span></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"product-name\">Windsurf</span> — Version 1.9600.40: GPT-5.4 Mini Integration\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Added GPT-5.4 mini model support for faster, more efficient code completion and generation tasks.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Release</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-06</span></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"product-name\">Windsurf</span> — Version 1.9600.38: Adaptive Model\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Introduced Adaptive Model feature that dynamically selects the most appropriate AI model based on task complexity and context.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Feature</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-06</span></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span> — Unified Request-Based Pricing Model\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Cursor simplified pricing to a unified request-based model, replacing previous complex tier structures.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Announcement</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-01</span></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span> — Memories Feature: Context Persistence\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Memories feature allows Cursor to remember important project context and user preferences across sessions for more personalized assistance.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Feature</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-01</span></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span> — Jupyter Notebook Support\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Added support for Jupyter Notebook files with enhanced editing and AI assistance capabilities for data science workflows.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Feature</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-01</span></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span> — One-Click MCP Server Installation\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simplified installation process for MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers with a single click, reducing setup complexity for external tool integrations.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Feature</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-01</span></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span> — BugBot: Automatic PR Review Agent\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        BugBot provides automated pull request review capabilities, identifying issues and suggesting fixes before merge.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Feature</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-01</span></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span> — Background Agents in Slack Integration\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Cursor now supports launching Background Agents directly from Slack by mentioning @Cursor, enabling AI-powered workflows within team communication channels.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Feature</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-01</span></div>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"feedback-section\">\n                        <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"I wish they'd keep the old philosophy of letting the developer drive and the agent assist. I still want to _code_, not vibe my way through tickets.\"</div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback-source\">\n                            — Medium <span class=\"feedback-sentiment sentiment-negative\">Negative</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n            <section class=\"section\" id=\"insights\">\n                <div class=\"section-header\">Technical Insights</div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-discussion\">Discussion</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/2/lenny-podcast-highlights/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Agentic Engineering Conversation Highlights</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon Willison on Lenny's Podcast covering agentic engineering, coding agents, and the state of AI in 2026.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison / Lenny Rachitsky</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">agentic-engineering</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">automation</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/2/gemma-4/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Gemma 4: Most Capable Open Models</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Google released four new vision-capable Apache 2.0 licensed reasoning LLMs (2B, 4B, 31B, plus 26B-A4B MoE). Native video, images, and audio processing.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-02</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">gemma-4</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">open-models</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">vision-llms</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/3/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">AI-Generated Security Reports: From Slop to Real Research</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Linux kernel security list went from 2-3 reports/week to 5-10/day with most being correct. Different AI tools finding same bugs.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Greg Kroah-Hartman, Daniel Stenberg, Willy Tarreau | 2026-04-03</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">ai-security-research</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">vulnerability-research</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">linux-kernel</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/3/vulnerability-research-cooked/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Vulnerability Research Transformed by AI</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Thomas Ptacek: Within months, agents will find zero-days by pointing at source trees. LLMs uniquely suited for pattern-matching and constraint-solving.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Thomas Ptacek | 2026-04-03</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">ai-security-research</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">vulnerability-research</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/4/github-growth/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Activity Surging: 275M Commits/Week</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        GitHub COO: 275M commits/week, on pace for 14B in 2026. GitHub Actions grew from 500M minutes/week (2023) to 2.1B minutes in one week.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Kyle Daigle (GitHub COO) | 2026-04-04</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">github</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">github-actions</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">platform-metrics</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/research-llm-apis/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">LLM Provider HTTP APIs Research</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon Willison researching new abstraction layer for LLM library. Scripts and outputs for Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, and Mistral raw JSON APIs.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-05</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">llm</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">apis</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/scan-for-secrets/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">scan-for-secrets: Tool to Scan Files Before Sharing</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Python tool v0.1 to scan files for secrets before publishing. Built with Claude Code using README-driven-development. CLI and Python API.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-05</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">agentic-engineering</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/syntaqlite-playground/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Syntaqlite Playground: SQLite Validation in Browser</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Web-based playground for syntaqlite SQLite linting tool. UI for formatting, parsing AST, validating, tokenizing queries using WebAssembly/Pyodide.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison / Lalit Maganti | 2026-04-05</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">sqlite</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">sql</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">tools</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/eight-years-three-months/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Eight Years Wanting, Three Months Building with AI</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Lalit Maganti built syntaqlite SQLite parser in 3 months with Claude Code after procrastinating 8 years. AI excels at concrete problems but struggles with design decisions.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Lalit Maganti | 2026-04-05</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">sqlite</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">vibe-coding</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">architecture</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/chatgpt-healthcare/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">ChatGPT Healthcare Usage Insights from OpenAI</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        ~2M weekly messages on health insurance, ~600K from people in 'hospital deserts' (30 min drive to nearest hospital). 7/10 messages outside clinic hours.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Chengpeng Mou (OpenAI) | 2026-04-05</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">openai</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">chatgpt</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">healthcare</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">llms</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/6/datasette-ports/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">datasette-ports: Find Running Datasette Instances</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Tool to solve losing track of multiple Datasette instances. 'datasette ports' lists all running instances with URLs, versions, databases, and plugins.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-06</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">datasette</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">developer-tools</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">python</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/6/cleanup-claude-code-paste/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Cleanup Claude Code Paste Tool</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon Willison created web tool to clean up prompts copied from Claude Code terminal. Removes '❯' prompt, fixes wrapped-line whitespace, copy-to-clipboard button.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-06</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">tools</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <footer>\n        <p>Agentic Coding Research Report | Generated on April 13, 2026</p>\n        <p>\n            <a href=\"#\">Archive</a> ·\n            <a href=\"#\">About</a> ·\n            <a href=\"#\">RSS Feed</a> ·\n            <a href=\"#\">GitHub</a>\n        </p>\n    </footer>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
